WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.987
[MUSIC]

00:00:10.987 --> 00:00:16.089
One of the research projects at the
Stanford Rock Center, is taking a look

00:00:16.089 --> 00:00:21.380
at the role of social media in, for senior
executives, and board members.

00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:25.340
What we've done is a survey of a couple
hundred senior executives and board

00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:30.220
members, asking them questions about, how
well do you understand social media?

00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:32.260
Do you, do you use it personally?

00:00:32.260 --> 00:00:36.250
And also, you know, what are you actually
doing in the company?

00:00:36.250 --> 00:00:37.550
Are you collecting this information?

00:00:37.550 --> 00:00:39.250
Where does it go?

00:00:39.250 --> 00:00:40.280
Are you using it?

00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:42.190
Do you find it valuable, and things like
that.

00:00:42.190 --> 00:00:48.170
One of the key findings is that most of
the companies are using social media,

00:00:48.170 --> 00:00:50.790
but it really doesn't get up to the senior
level or Board level.

00:00:50.790 --> 00:00:52.620
It's basically used for

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:56.780
customer, outreach, a bit of marketing,
things like that.

00:00:56.780 --> 00:01:00.660
At the Board level, you know, you know,
very, very little.

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:05.450
I mean, the, sort of the verbatim
responses that we got were, this is new.

00:01:05.450 --> 00:01:07.190
We're not sure what it is.

00:01:07.190 --> 00:01:08.540
Seems interesting.

00:01:08.540 --> 00:01:11.350
It's like, you know, is this just another
flash in the pan.

00:01:11.350 --> 00:01:14.360
I think the social media thing scares
companies as well.

00:01:14.360 --> 00:01:18.680
They've seen certain things go viral,
typically viral in a bad way.

00:01:18.680 --> 00:01:22.910
What happened, you know, why couldn't we
have controlled that, that kinda thing.

00:01:22.910 --> 00:01:27.960
It's a new, technology that they're
actually not that familiar with,

00:01:27.960 --> 00:01:30.590
it's hard for them to think through the
ramifications of it.

00:01:30.590 --> 00:01:33.950
I think it's also hard for them to say,
okay, if we do this,

00:01:33.950 --> 00:01:36.680
you know, is there a business case to be
made?

00:01:36.680 --> 00:01:39.330
Are we sure that this is value accretive
or not.

00:01:40.970 --> 00:01:45.720
From our side, we think it is a valuable,
place for information.

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:49.980
There's a lot of topics in social media
that are,

00:01:49.980 --> 00:01:54.650
that map directly into high level
management and, and, board structure.

00:01:54.650 --> 00:01:58.730
I think one of the key ones, is all the
elements of risk management.

00:01:58.730 --> 00:02:02.710
You hear things that are, that are coming
months, or maybe years ahead of time.

00:02:02.710 --> 00:02:07.270
That would help you manage a reputation of
the organization, and at the board level,

00:02:07.270 --> 00:02:11.490
you know, worry about risks that sometimes
you get blindsided by.

00:02:11.490 --> 00:02:15.810
I think it is inevitable that it's gotta
have an impact on, on, companies.

00:02:15.810 --> 00:02:19.590
You know, how they attach to their
employees, how they attach to suppliers.

00:02:19.590 --> 00:02:21.640
There's [INAUDIBLE] attached to customers.

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:25.610
We're still trying to figure out, you
know, what are, what are the steps.

00:02:25.610 --> 00:02:28.510
Lots of the companies that do this are
collecting and analyzing and

00:02:28.510 --> 00:02:33.000
tracking data, and providing, you know,
strategies around, around social media.

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:35.540
What happens when that information is
inside the organization?

00:02:35.540 --> 00:02:36.730
What does it do?

00:02:36.730 --> 00:02:38.900
What it, what processes are changed?

00:02:38.900 --> 00:02:41.170
You know, can you show that value's being
created?

00:02:41.170 --> 00:02:42.310
That's really why we did the survey.

00:02:42.310 --> 00:02:46.433
What are people doing, people are making
decisions,

00:02:46.433 --> 00:02:49.934
how informed are they, and things like
that.

00:02:49.934 --> 00:02:58.869
[BLANK_AUDIO]

